// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:39
//
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:40
//
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:41
//# Page 37
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:42
//# CONVENTIONS AND NOTATIONS UTILIZED FOR ERASABLE ASSIGNMENTS.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:43
//
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:44
//#	EQUALS	IS USED IN TWO WAYS.  IT IS OFTEN USED TO CHAIN A GROUP
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:45
//#		OF ASSIGNMENTS SO THAT THE GROUP MAY BE MOVED WITH THE
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:46
//#		CHANGING OF ONLY ONE CARD.  EXAMPLE:
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:47
//#
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:48
//#			X	EQUALS	START
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:49
//#			Y	EQUALS	X	+SIZE.X
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:50
//#			Z	EQUALS	Y	+SIZE.Y
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:51
//#
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:52
//#		(X, Y, AND Z ARE CONSECUTIVE AND BEGIN AT START.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:53
//#		SIZE.X AND SIZE.Y ARE THE RESPECTIVE SIZES OF X AND Y.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:54
//#		USUALLY NUMERIC, IE. 1, 2, 6, 18D, ETC.)
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:55
//
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:56
//#	EQUALS	OFTEN IMPLIES THE SHARING OF REGISTERS (DIFFERENT NAMES
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:57
//#		AND DIFFERENT DATA).  EXAMPLE:
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:58
//#
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:59
//#			X	EQUALS	Y
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:60
//
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:61
//#	=	MEANS THAT MULTIPLE NAMES HAVE BEEN GIVEN TO THE SAME DATA.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:62
//#		(THIS IS LOGICAL EQUIVALENCE, NOT SHARING.)  EXAMPLE:
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:63
//#
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:64
//#			X	=	Y
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:65
//
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:66
//#	THE SIE AND UTILIZATION OF AN ERASABLE ARE OFTEN INCLUDED IN
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:67
//#	THE COMMENTS IN THE FOLLOWING FORM:  M(SIZE)N.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:68
//#
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:69
//#		M	REFERS TO THE MOBILITY OF THE ASSIGNMENT.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:70
//#			B	MEANS THAT THE SYMBOL IS REFERENCED BY BASIC
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:71
//#				INSTRUCTIONS AND THUS IS E-BANK SENSITIVE.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:72
//#			I	MEANS THAT THE SYMBOL IS REFERENCED ONLY BY
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:73
//#				INTERPRETIVE INSTRUCTIONS, AND IS THUS E-BANK
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:74
//#				INSENSITIVE AND MAY APPEAR IN ANY E-BANK.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:75
//#
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:76
//#		SIZE	IS THE NUMBER OF REGISTERS INCLUDED BY THE SYMBOL.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:77
//#
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:78
//#		N	INDICATES THE NATURE OF PERMANENCE OF THE CONTENTS.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:79
//#			PL	MEANS THAT THE CONTENTS ARE PAD LOADED.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:80
//#			DSP	MEANS THAT THE REGISTER IS USED FOR A DISPLAY.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:81
//#			PRM	MEANS THAT THE REGISTER IS PERMANENT.  IE., IT
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:82
//#				IS USED DURING THE ENTIRE MISSION FOR ONE
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:83
//#				PURPOSE AND CANNOT BE SHARED.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:84
//#			TMP	MEANS THAT THE REGISTER IS USED TEMPORARILY OR
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:85
//#				IS A SCRATCH REGISTER FOR THE ROUTINE TO WHICH
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:86
//#				IT IS ASSIGNED.  THAT IS, IT NEED NOT BE SET
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:87
//#				PRIOR TO INVOCATION OF THE ROUTINE NOR DOES IT
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:88
//#				CONTAIN USEFUL OUTPUT TO ANOTHER ROUTINE.  THUS
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:89
//# Page 38
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:90
//#				IT MAY BE SHARED WITH ANY OTHER ROUTINE WHICH
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:91
//#				IS NOT ACTIVE IN PARALLEL
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:92
//#			IN	MEANS INPUT TO THE ROUTINE AND IT IS PROBABLY
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:93
//#				TEMPORARY FOR A HIGHER-LEVEL ROUTINE/PROGRAM.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:94
//#			OUT	MEANS OUTPUT FROM THE ROUTINE, PROBABLY
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:95
//#				TEMPORARY FOR A HIGHER-LEVEL ROUTINE/PROGRAM.
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:96
//
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:97
//# Page 39
// ERASABLE_ASSIGNMENTS.agc:98
//
